    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "For all its thematic complexity and literary prowess, Asian-American literature continues to be categorized and dismissed as cultural artifact.  Unfortunately, the application of critical literary theory within the context of Asian-American works remains largely incomplete.  In this thesis, I approach three stories from Hisaye Yamamoto's anthology \"Seventeen Syllables\" through the lens of critical feminist and historicist theory.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
